.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH auth 1  "auth " 
.SH NAME
auth \- Authentication and credentials
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBauth\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Authentication and credentials
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
auth\-login(1)
Log in to a host
.TP
auth\-logout(1)
Remove stored credentials for the host
.TP
auth\-status(1)
Show the current authentication status
.TP
auth\-setup\-git(1)
Register `nub` as a git credential helper
.TP
auth\-git\-credential(1)
Git credential protocol entry point (invoked by git, not by users)
.TP
auth\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
